{
 "help": "usage: wgsextract info calculate-coverage [-h] [-r REGION] [--bins] [--with-bins] [--by BED]\n                                          [--min-depth N] [--format {tsv,parquet}] [--status]\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help            show this help message and exit\n  -r, --region REGION   Chromosomal region (e.g. chrM, chrY:10000-20000); with --by, declare the\n                        assessed scope (all targets must fit inside it); otherwise the whole\n                        alignment header is the assessed scope\n  --bins                Report exact per-contig depth 0, 1-3, 4-7 and 8+ breadth of the non-N\n                        bases in one streaming pass.\n  --with-bins           Also measure the --bins depth breadth and show its table in place of the\n                        coverage table, which info --detailed then shows; up-to-date whole-file\n                        reports are shown again instead of rescanned.\n  --by BED              Report depth per target of this BED (e.g. from 'panel bed'): mean, median\n                        and the fraction at >=10x, 20x, 30x and --min-depth, plus the on- versus\n                        off-target enrichment\n  --min-depth N         With --by, list targets whose mean depth is below this (default: 30)\n  --format {tsv,parquet}\n                        Also save the per-chromosome table and the QC stats as <input>_chromosomes\n                        and <input>_qc .tsv or .parquet (needs pyarrow); implies --detailed. With\n                        --bins or --by, that table's format instead\n  --status              Only report whether the --with-bins reports in --outdir are newer than the\n                        input (current), so a run would show them again\n\nglobal options:\n  -i/--input, -o/--outdir, --genome, --ref, -t/--threads, -m/--memory, --json, --quiet, --debug,\n  --config and the other global options are accepted before or after the command; 'wgsextract\n  --help' lists them all.\n\nexamples:\n  wgsextract info calculate-coverage --input sample.cram\n  wgsextract info calculate-coverage --input sample.cram --bins --format parquet\n  wgsextract info calculate-coverage --input sample.bam --by panel.bed --min-depth 20\n  wgsextract info calculate-coverage --input sample.cram --status\n\noutputs (in the output directory unless noted):\n  <input file name>_coverage.tsv, or with --bins <input file\n  name>_coverage_bins.tsv (depth bands, or .parquet with --format parquet)\n  instead; with --with-bins both .tsv files. With --by,\n  <input>_<bed>_target_coverage.tsv (depth per target) and\n  <input>_<bed>_target_summary.txt (on- and off-target depth, enrichment and\n  targets below --min-depth). --status writes nothing.\n\nneeds:\n  samtools; depending on options and inputs, also: bcftools; minutes on a 30x\n  genome.\n",
